.TH ESDM\-GETRAWENTROPY 8 "2026-08-05" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
esdm\-getrawentropy \- read raw noise source data from the ESDM kernel module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esdm\-getrawentropy
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esdm\-getrawentropy
reads raw, unconditioned noise source samples from a debugfs interface of the
.I linux_esdm_es
kernel add\-on and writes them as decimal ASCII, one 64 bit sample per line \-
the input format of
.BR esdm\-extractlsb (8).
It is the first step of an SP800\-90B entropy assessment of the kernel based
interrupt and scheduler entropy sources.
.PP
The kernel module exports one file per source below
.IR /sys/kernel/debug/esdm_es/ ,
and it only does so when built with its testing support. Reading debugfs
requires root.
.PP
This tool is built with the meson option
.BR validation\-helpers .
It is for measurement and validation only and has no place in a production
deployment. For the eBPF based entropy sources, which have no debugfs
interface, use
.BR esdm\-ebpf\-collect (8)
instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-samples " \fINUM\fR"
Number of samples to collect. Default: 1000. An SP800\-90B assessment needs at
least 1,000,000.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-debugfs\-file " \fIFILE\fR"
Interface to read from. Default:
.IR /sys/kernel/debug/esdm_es/esdm_raw_sched_hires ,
the high\-resolution time stamps of the scheduler entropy source. The interrupt
entropy source is
.I /sys/kernel/debug/esdm_es/esdm_raw_hires
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-outfile " \fIFILE\fR"
Write to
.I FILE
instead of standard output. The file must not exist \- an existing one is not
overwritten, so a collection cannot silently clobber an earlier one.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit with a non\-zero status.
.SH OUTPUT
One decimal sample per line on standard output or in the output file. Progress
is reported on standard error, so redirecting standard output keeps the data
clean.
.SH EXAMPLES
The three steps of an assessment, using the NIST
SP800\-90B_EntropyAssessment tools:
.PP
.RS
.nf
esdm\-getrawentropy \-s 1000000 \-o /tmp/data\-0001.out
esdm\-extractlsb /tmp/data\-0001.out /tmp/data\-0001.extracted.out 1000000 FF
ea_non_iid /tmp/data\-0001.extracted.out 8
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
This tool is taken from the LRNG project and adapted, see
.I https://github.com/smuellerDD/lrng/tree/master/test/sp80090b
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esdm\-extractlsb (8),
.BR esdm\-ebpf\-collect (8),
.BR esdm\-server (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Stephan Mueller <smueller@chronox.de>
